API-18: document EN_TANKLEVEL as the initial level; read reservoir head

EN_getnodevalue(EN_TANKLEVEL) returns a tank's initial water level, as
the maintainers ruled in PR #633, but the enum comment still called it
the "current computed tank water level (read only)" and the toolkit
guide listed it among computed results. Correct both, and say how to
get the current level. For a reservoir, EN_setnodevalue(EN_TANKLEVEL)
sets the head, but the getter returned 0; return the head instead.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-18_fix.patch

